# This .gitignore file is designed to maintain a clean and professional repository
# structure for a Python-based development workflow that includes Jupyter notebooks,
# data science experiments, and macOS environments. It excludes automatically
# generated files such as Python bytecode caches, notebook checkpoint directories,
# and macOS system artifacts that do not belong in version control. 
#
# In addition, it ignores build outputs, package distribution folders, virtual
# environment directories, and IDE/editor-specific settings (e.g., VS Code and
# IntelliJ). These files are machine-specific and would otherwise clutter commit
# history or cause inconsistencies across different development environments.
#
# Temporary logs and miscellaneous runtime files are also excluded to prevent
# accidental commits of transient or debug-related artifacts. By filtering out
# these non-essential files, the repository remains lightweight, reproducible, and
# collaborative-friendly, ensuring that only meaningful source code and relevant
# project assets are tracked in Git.

# ===== Python cache =====
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ===== Jupyter notebooks =====
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# ===== macOS system files =====
.DS_Store

# ===== Build artifacts =====
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# ===== Virtual environments =====
.venv/
venv/
env/

# ===== Editor settings =====
.vscode/
.idea/

# ===== Misc =====
*.log
*.tmp
